      ],
      "source": "https://www.virginiabeachhistory.org/timeline",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1915, the Star of the Sea Catholic Church was founded on Groves land, adding a new spiritual landmark to Bayside.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.virginiabeachhistory.org/timeline",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Willis Hodges, a free Negro, was arrested in 1844 for “unlawfully preaching” but was unanimously acquitted, marking an early civil‑rights moment in Bayside.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
